{
  "name": "veriflow-agency",
  "displayName": "Agency",
  "description": "Specialists you hire into your repository. Pull request reviews with evidence-backed findings, triage right next to the code, and measurable precision.",
  "version": "0.3.1",
  "publisher": "veriflow",
  "license": "UNLICENSED",
  "private": true,
  "engines": {
    "vscode": "^1.85.0"
  },
  "categories": [
    "Other",
    "Linters"
  ],
  "keywords": [
    "code review",
    "pull request",
    "triage"
  ],
  "main": "./src/extension.js",
  "activationEvents": [
    "onStartupFinished"
  ],
  "scripts": {
    "package": "node -e \"require('fs').mkdirSync('../../dist',{recursive:true})\" && npx --yes @vscode/vsce package --no-dependencies --allow-missing-repository --out ../../dist/",
    "test": "node test/harness.js"
  },
  "contributes": {
    "viewsContainers": {
      "activitybar": [
        {
          "id": "agency",
          "title": "Agency",
          "icon": "resources/agency.svg"
        }
      ]
    },
    "views": {
      "agency": [
        {
          "id": "agency.overview",
          "name": "Overview",
          "icon": "$(dashboard)"
        },
        {
          "id": "agency.findings",
          "name": "Findings",
          "icon": "$(inbox)"
        },
        {
          "id": "agency.runs",
          "name": "Runs",
          "icon": "$(history)",
          "visibility": "collapsed"
        },
        {
          "id": "agency.tools",
          "name": "Specialists",
          "icon": "$(person)",
          "visibility": "collapsed"
        }
      ]
    },
    "viewsWelcome": [
      {
        "view": "agency.overview",
        "when": "!agency.ready && agency.reason == no-folder",
        "contents": "Agency works inside a project.\n\nOpen a folder with a git repository and this panel fills itself in.\n\n[Open folder](command:vscode.openFolder)"
      },
      {
        "view": "agency.overview",
        "when": "!agency.ready && agency.reason == no-cli",
        "contents": "The core is missing.\n\nThe extension is only a client — all the work is done by the `agency` command, the same one an agent calls from the terminal.\n\nInstall it:\n\n```\nuv tool install --editable <veriflow-agency>/packages/core\n```\n\n[Set the path to agency](command:agency.openSettings)\n[Try again](command:agency.refresh)"
      },
      {
        "view": "agency.overview",
        "when": "!agency.ready && agency.reason == no-repo",
        "contents": "There is no git repository here.\n\nFindings are stored in `.agency/` inside the project so they survive a reinstall and a fresh clone — without a repository there is nowhere to put them.\n\n[Try again](command:agency.refresh)"
      },
      {
        "view": "agency.overview",
        "when": "!agency.ready && agency.reason == error",
        "contents": "Agency failed to start. The details are in Output → Agency.\n\n[Check prerequisites](command:agency.doctor)\n[Try again](command:agency.refresh)"
      },
      {
        "view": "agency.findings",
        "when": "agency.ready && !agency.hasRuns",
        "contents": "No run yet.\n\nTwo specialists, two ways of finding a problem.\n\nThe reviewer walks a pull request and cross-checks the changes against the real structure of the code.\n\n[Review a pull request](command:agency.review.pick)\n\nThe QA engineer explores the running application following a brief you write, reproduces every problem from a clean session and anchors it to the code that causes it.\n\n[Start a QA session](command:agency.qa.run)\n\nEither of them can be hired on more than one AI runner and started side by side on the same code — they share the findings, so the second one's repeats are marked as duplicates rather than asked about twice.\n\nA run starts in a visible terminal, not in the background: attended is a property of the system, not an intention."
      },
      {
        "view": "agency.findings",
        "when": "agency.ready && agency.hasRuns && !agency.hasFindings",
        "contents": "The run finished, but the findings are not here yet.\n\nThe agent writes `findings.json` when it is done. After that they have to be pulled through the gate — it checks the contract, that the files exist, and duplicates.\n\n[Process run output](command:agency.ingest)\n[Review another PR](command:agency.review.pick)"
      },
      {
        "view": "agency.tools",
        "when": "agency.ready",
        "contents": "A specialist is a **method** plus the **runner** that follows it.\n\nHiring one brings its procedure and its configuration into the project; rules and documentation stay with the project.\n\nThe same method can be hired once per runner — a reviewer on Claude and a reviewer on Codex share one configuration, one queue of findings and one dedup, and can walk the same pull request side by side.\n\n[Hire a specialist](command:agency.hire.add)\n[Register an AI runner](command:agency.provider.add)"
      }
    ],
    "configuration": {
      "title": "Agency",
      "properties": {
        "agency.cliPath": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "agency",
          "markdownDescription": "Path to the `agency` command. Leave it as `agency` when it is on PATH; `uv tool install` can also put it somewhere else.",
          "order": 1
        },
        "agency.pack": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "review-graph",
          "description": "Deprecated — the roster decides who runs (`agency roster`). Kept so an older setting does not break; it is ignored when the project has hired specialists.",
          "order": 2
        },
        "agency.model": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "default": null,
          "markdownDescription": "Fallback model for a project with no roster. Empty = the model of the specialist that takes the run.\n\nThe model is a property of the task, not of the user: a review is reading and classification, not writing, so it can run cheaper than coding. Per specialist it is set by `agency hire <pack> --model <m>`, and the choice is written into the run record so you can measure which one produces better findings.",
          "order": 3
        },
        "agency.provider": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ],
          "default": null,
          "markdownDescription": "Fallback runner for a project with no roster. Empty = the runner of the specialist that takes the run. Runners are registered per machine — `agency providers`.",
          "order": 4
        },
        "agency.commentThreads": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": true,
          "markdownDescription": "Show findings as comments right at the line of code. Turning this off leaves only the Agency panel.",
          "order": 5
        },
        "agency.autoRefresh": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": true,
          "markdownDescription": "Reload when `.agency/runs/` changes from the outside — that is, when an agent or a terminal decides. Turning this off means changes only show up after a manual refresh.",
          "order": 6
        }
      }
    },
    "submenus": [
      {
        "id": "agency.rejectMenu",
        "label": "Reject",
        "icon": "$(circle-slash)"
      }
    ],
    "commands": [
      {
        "command": "agency.review.pick",
        "title": "Review a pull request…",
        "category": "Agency",
        "icon": "$(play)"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.qa.run",
        "title": "Start a QA session…",
        "category": "Agency",
        "icon": "$(beaker)"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.chain.run",
        "title": "Run a team…",
        "category": "Agency",
        "icon": "$(organization)"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.ingest",
        "title": "Process run output",
        "category": "Agency",
        "icon": "$(filter)"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.run.close",
        "title": "Close run",
        "category": "Agency",
        "icon": "$(stop-circle)"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.run.discard",
        "title": "Discard run",
        "category": "Agency",
        "icon": "$(trash)"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.refresh",
        "title": "Reload",
        "category": "Agency",
        "icon": "$(refresh)"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.doctor",
        "title": "Check prerequisites",
        "category": "Agency",
        "icon": "$(pulse)"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.metrics",
        "title": "Metrics — precision, dedup, queue",
        "category": "Agency",
        "icon": "$(graph)"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.openSettings",
        "title": "Settings",
        "category": "Agency",
        "icon": "$(settings-gear)"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.pack.add",
        "title": "Hire a specialist…",
        "category": "Agency",
        "icon": "$(person-add)"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.hire.add",
        "title": "Hire a specialist…",
        "category": "Agency",
        "icon": "$(person-add)"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.hire.remove",
        "title": "Dismiss this specialist",
        "category": "Agency",
        "icon": "$(trash)"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.hire.run",
        "title": "Run this specialist…",
        "category": "Agency",
        "icon": "$(play)"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.provider.add",
        "title": "Register an AI runner…",
        "category": "Agency",
        "icon": "$(rocket)"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.view.tools.focus",
        "title": "Go to the specialists",
        "category": "Agency"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.pack.openConfig",
        "title": "Open pack configuration",
        "category": "Agency"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.finding.open",
        "title": "Open finding detail",
        "category": "Agency",
        "icon": "$(book)"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.finding.reveal",
        "title": "Show in code",
        "category": "Agency",
        "icon": "$(go-to-file)"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.finding.accept",
        "title": "Accept",
        "icon": "$(check)"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.finding.defer",
        "title": "Defer for later",
        "icon": "$(bookmark)"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.finding.reject.not-reproducible",
        "title": "Could not reproduce"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.finding.reject.by-design",
        "title": "Behaves that way by design"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.finding.reject.wrong-diagnosis",
        "title": "Wrong diagnosis — the problem is elsewhere"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.finding.reject.duplicate-missed",
        "title": "Duplicate the dedup missed"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.finding.reject.out-of-scope",
        "title": "Out of scope for this project"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.finding.rejectPick",
        "title": "Reject…",
        "icon": "$(circle-slash)"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.finding.addNote",
        "title": "Save note"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.finding.openAtCommit",
        "title": "Show the code as of the analysis",
        "icon": "$(history)"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.finding.diffAgainstHead",
        "title": "Compare with the working tree",
        "icon": "$(git-compare)"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.decision.apply",
        "title": "Record a decision (programmatically)",
        "category": "Agency"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.view.findings.focus",
        "title": "Go to the findings queue",
        "category": "Agency"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.pack.brief",
        "title": "Set the standing brief…",
        "category": "Agency",
        "icon": "$(note)"
      },
      {
        "command": "agency.qa.playwright",
        "title": "Browser testing setup…",
        "category": "Agency",
        "icon": "$(browser)"
      }
    ],
    "menus": {
      "commandPalette": [
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.accept",
          "when": "false"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.defer",
          "when": "false"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.rejectPick",
          "when": "false"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.addNote",
          "when": "false"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.reject.not-reproducible",
          "when": "false"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.reject.by-design",
          "when": "false"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.reject.wrong-diagnosis",
          "when": "false"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.reject.duplicate-missed",
          "when": "false"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.reject.out-of-scope",
          "when": "false"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.openAtCommit",
          "when": "false"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.diffAgainstHead",
          "when": "false"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.open",
          "when": "false"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.reveal",
          "when": "false"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.pack.openConfig",
          "when": "false"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.decision.apply",
          "when": "false"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.view.findings.focus",
          "when": "false"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.hire.remove",
          "when": "false"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.view.tools.focus",
          "when": "false"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.pack.add",
          "when": "false"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.run.discard",
          "when": "false"
        }
      ],
      "view/title": [
        {
          "command": "agency.review.pick",
          "group": "navigation@1",
          "when": "view == agency.overview || view == agency.runs"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.qa.run",
          "group": "navigation@2",
          "when": "view == agency.overview || view == agency.runs"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.chain.run",
          "group": "navigation@3",
          "when": "view == agency.overview || view == agency.runs"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.ingest",
          "group": "navigation@4",
          "when": "view == agency.runs"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.metrics",
          "group": "navigation@1",
          "when": "view == agency.findings"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.refresh",
          "group": "navigation@8",
          "when": "view == agency.overview || view == agency.findings"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.hire.add",
          "group": "navigation@1",
          "when": "view == agency.tools"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.doctor",
          "group": "1_check@1",
          "when": "view == agency.overview"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.openSettings",
          "group": "9_config@1",
          "when": "view == agency.overview || view == agency.tools"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.pack.brief",
          "group": "9_config@2",
          "when": "view == agency.tools"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.qa.playwright",
          "group": "9_config@3",
          "when": "view == agency.tools"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.provider.add",
          "group": "9_config@4",
          "when": "view == agency.tools"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.run.close",
          "group": "navigation@3",
          "when": "view == agency.runs"
        }
      ],
      "view/item/context": [
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.accept",
          "group": "inline@1",
          "when": "viewItem == agencyFinding.open"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.rejectPick",
          "group": "inline@2",
          "when": "viewItem == agencyFinding.open"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.reveal",
          "group": "inline@3",
          "when": "viewItem =~ /^agencyFinding/"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.defer",
          "group": "1_decide@1",
          "when": "viewItem == agencyFinding.open"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.openAtCommit",
          "group": "2_look@1",
          "when": "viewItem =~ /^agencyFinding/"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.diffAgainstHead",
          "group": "2_look@2",
          "when": "viewItem =~ /^agencyFinding/"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.hire.add",
          "group": "inline@1",
          "when": "viewItem == agencyPack.available"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.hire.run",
          "group": "inline@1",
          "when": "viewItem == agencyHire"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.hire.add",
          "group": "1_hire@1",
          "when": "viewItem == agencyHire"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.pack.brief",
          "group": "1_hire@2",
          "when": "viewItem == agencyHire"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.hire.remove",
          "group": "inline@2",
          "when": "viewItem == agencyHire"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.run.close",
          "group": "inline@1",
          "when": "viewItem == agencyRun.open"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.run.discard",
          "group": "9_remove@1",
          "when": "viewItem =~ /^agencyRun/"
        }
      ],
      "comments/commentThread/title": [
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.accept",
          "group": "inline@1",
          "when": "commentController == agency.findings"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.defer",
          "group": "inline@2",
          "when": "commentController == agency.findings"
        },
        {
          "submenu": "agency.rejectMenu",
          "group": "inline@3",
          "when": "commentController == agency.findings"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.open",
          "group": "inline@4",
          "when": "commentController == agency.findings"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.openAtCommit",
          "group": "inline@5",
          "when": "commentController == agency.findings"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.diffAgainstHead",
          "group": "inline@6",
          "when": "commentController == agency.findings && commentThread == agencyFinding.drifted"
        }
      ],
      "agency.rejectMenu": [
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.reject.not-reproducible",
          "group": "1_reasons@1"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.reject.by-design",
          "group": "1_reasons@2"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.reject.wrong-diagnosis",
          "group": "1_reasons@3"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.reject.duplicate-missed",
          "group": "1_reasons@4"
        },
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.reject.out-of-scope",
          "group": "1_reasons@5"
        }
      ],
      "comments/commentThread/context": [
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.addNote",
          "group": "inline@1",
          "when": "commentController == agency.findings"
        }
      ],
      "comments/comment/context": [
        {
          "command": "agency.finding.rejectPick",
          "group": "inline@1",
          "when": "commentController == agency.findings"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
